    body: 'Food Safety Officer roles under state Food Safety departments (recruited via state PSCs and occasionally SSC), plus private-sector food-safety compliance, licensing, and audit roles that sit between a company and the regulator. Steady, government-adjacent, and consistently in demand as India tightens food-safety enforcement — but recruitment cycles are irregular and competitive.',
  },
  {
    label: 'Quality',
    title: 'QA/QC roles inside FMCG and food manufacturing',
    body: 'The largest single employer lane for food-tech graduates: incoming-material checks, in-process quality control, HACCP and ISO 22000 compliance, batch release, and audit readiness at plants run by Nestlé, ITC, Britannia, Hindustan Unilever, and hundreds of smaller regional and contract manufacturers. High volume of openings; the honest trade-off is a modest starting floor and heavy documentation and shift-adjacent plant work in the early years.',
